; 07-instantiate-a-universal-fact.kurt
;
; Instantiate a universal fact
;
; Load `logic` for quantifier inference rules. A universally quantified fact can be instantiated
; at a particular value:

load logic
prop P
const P, c

use forall x P(x)
P(c)

; `x` is the bound variable of the quantifier: it needs no declaration and no sigil, and it doesn't
; become a constant. (A `$` or `%` sigil marks a *free* variable, as in a rule `use $a + 0 = $a`
; (see keywords/06-var.kurt); a bound variable doesn't need one.) Instantiating a universal fact is built
; into Kurt, so `P(c)` follows directly from the fact and the output shows just `by` and the line of the fact.
